(Bug #59's second open question, answered. The register entry asked whether
 a `treating`-wrapped read carries the wrong type forward into an `is a`
 guard downstream. It did: the tag reaching a `value` parameter was the
 integer default, so `is a text` was false for a text element. The
 predicate reads the runtime tag (LANGUAGE.md:2419-2422), so once the
 clause keeps the tag the guard sees what the element really is - both for
 the element the clause replaced and for the one it left alone.)

To describe with a value called what.
  if what is a text, print "text: {what}",
  otherwise print "number: {what}".

describe of each item from [1, "a"] treating "a" as "b".
describe of each item from [1, "a"] treating 1 as 9.
